<PageTitle>@GlobalValues.CSS_Name_FocusOutline @GlobalValues.Common_Page_Title_Api_Usage</PageTitle>

<h1>@GlobalValues.CSS_Name_FocusOutline @GlobalValues.Common_Page_Title_Api_Usage</h1>

<p>
    Everything you need to work with the <span class="@CodeSpan.Base">br-focus-outline</span> CSS class: the BEM classes it provides, the strongly-typed <span class="@CodeSpan.Base">FocusOutline</span> C# object
    used to apply them, supporting enums, and the CSS variables used for styling.
</p>

<h2 class="mobile-centred-heading">Overview</h2>

<p>
    <span class="@CodeSpan.Base">br-focus-outline</span> is a behavioural utility class that draws a focus indicator from the
    <span class="@CodeSpan.Base">--br-unit-outline-*</span> and <span class="@CodeSpan.Base">--br-unit-outline-offset-*</span> primitive scales. By default the outline is only shown for
    keyboard and assistive-technology focus, using <span class="@CodeSpan.Base">:focus-visible</span> - clicking with a mouse won't trigger it.
</p>
<p>
    Colour, style, width and offset all default to the shared <span class="@CodeSpan.Base">--br-comp-all-outline-*</span> tokens, which are the same tokens every focusable
    component in Blazor Ramp uses for its own focus ring. Overriding those tokens changes the focus indicator everywhere at once; the width and offset
    modifiers below let you adjust an individual element without touching the shared tokens.
</p>
<p>
    Unlike <span class="@CodeSpan.Base">br-section</span>'s radius grouping, <span class="@CodeSpan.Base">br-focus-outline</span> has no themeable grouping to bypass - the width and offset
    modifiers always set a fixed value from the unit scale directly.
</p>

<section>
    <h2 id="c#-classes" class="mobile-centred-heading">C# API</h2>
    <p>
        <span class="@CodeSpan.Base">FocusOutline</span> provides the BEM CSS classes for the br-focus-outline block: a reusable
        focus indicator that can be composed onto any focusable element.
    </p>
    <section>
        <h3 id="focusoutline-class" class="mobile-centred-heading">FocusOutline class</h3>
        <div class="@Section.Base @Section.NoPadding @Section.OverflowX(UnitScroll.Auto) @Padding.Block(UnitSpace.Four)">
            <table class="@Table.Base @Table.CodeTable" tabindex="0" aria-labelledby="focusoutline-class">
                <thead>
                    <tr>
                        <th scope="col">Return</th>
                        <th scope="col">Const/Static Method</th>
                        <th scope="col">Description</th>
                    </tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody>
                    <tr>
                        <td>string</td>
                        <td>FocusOutline.Base</td>
                        <td>The base class, <span class="@CodeSpan.Base">br-focus-outline</span>. Always required.</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                        <td>string</td>
                        <td>FocusOutline.Off</td>
                        <td>Suppresses the focus outline entirely, for both mouse and keyboard focus.</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                        <td>string</td>
                        <td>FocusOutline.OnFocus</td>
                        <td>
                            Shows the outline on any focus, not just keyboard/assistive-technology
                            focus. Use sparingly - this reintroduces the outline for mouse users too.
                        </td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                        <td>string</td>
                        <td>FocusOutline.Width(UnitOutlineWidth unitOutlineWidth)</td>
                        <td>Gets the class that sets the focus outline's width.</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                        <td>string</td>
                        <td>FocusOutline.Offset(UnitOutlineOffset unitOutlineOffset)</td>
                        <td>Gets the class that sets the focus outline's offset from the element's edge.</td>
                    </tr>
                </tbody>
            </table>
        </div>
    </section>
</section>

<section>
    <h2 class="mobile-centred-heading">Supporting enums</h2>
    <section>
        <h3 id="unit-outline-width-enum" class="mobile-centred-heading">UnitOutlineWidth enum</h3>
        <p>
            Sets the width of a <span class="@CodeSpan.Base">br-focus-outline</span> element's outline from the <span class="@CodeSpan.Base">--br-unit-outline-*</span> primitive scale.
        </p>
        <div class="@Section.Base @Section.NoPadding @Section.OverflowX(UnitScroll.Auto) @Padding.Block(UnitSpace.Four)">
            <table class="@Table.Base @Table.CodeTable" tabindex="0" aria-labelledby="unit-outline-width-enum">
                <thead>
                    <tr>
                        <th scope="col">Value</th>
                        <th scope="col">Name</th>
                        <th scope="col">Description</th>
                    </tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody>
                    <tr>
                        <td>0</td>
                        <td>None</td>
                        <td>No outline width. Maps to <span class="@CodeSpan.Base">--br-unit-outline-0</span>.</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                        <td>1</td>
                        <td>One</td>
                        <td>Maps to <span class="@CodeSpan.Base">--br-unit-outline-1</span>.</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                        <td>2</td>
                        <td>Two</td>
                        <td>Maps to <span class="@CodeSpan.Base">--br-unit-outline-2</span>. This is the library's default outline width.</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                        <td>3</td>
                        <td>Three</td>
                        <td>Maps to <span class="@CodeSpan.Base">--br-unit-outline-3</span>.</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                        <td>4</td>
                        <td>Four</td>
                        <td>Maps to <span class="@CodeSpan.Base">--br-unit-outline-4</span>.</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                        <td>5</td>
                        <td>Five</td>
                        <td>Maps to <span class="@CodeSpan.Base">--br-unit-outline-5</span>.</td>
                    </tr>
                </tbody>
            </table>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section>
        <h3 id="unit-outline-offset-enum" class="mobile-centred-heading">UnitOutlineOffset enum</h3>
        <p>
            Sets the offset of a <span class="@CodeSpan.Base">br-focus-outline</span> element's outline from the <span class="@CodeSpan.Base">--br-unit-outline-offset-*</span> primitive scale.
        </p>
        <div class="@Section.Base @Section.NoPadding @Section.OverflowX(UnitScroll.Auto) @Padding.Block(UnitSpace.Four)">
            <table class="@Table.Base @Table.CodeTable" tabindex="0" aria-labelledby="unit-outline-offset-enum">
                <thead>
                    <tr>
                        <th scope="col">Value</th>
                        <th scope="col">Name</th>
                        <th scope="col">Description</th>
                    </tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody>
                    <tr>
                        <td>0</td>
                        <td>None</td>
                        <td>No offset - the outline sits flush against the element's edge. Maps to <span class="@CodeSpan.Base">--br-unit-outline-offset-0</span>.</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                        <td>1</td>
                        <td>One</td>
                        <td>Maps to <span class="@CodeSpan.Base">--br-unit-outline-offset-1</span>.</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                        <td>2</td>
                        <td>Two</td>
                        <td>Maps to <span class="@CodeSpan.Base">--br-unit-outline-offset-2</span>. This is the library's default outline offset.</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                        <td>3</td>
                        <td>Three</td>
                        <td>Maps to <span class="@CodeSpan.Base">--br-unit-outline-offset-3</span>.</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                        <td>4</td>
                        <td>Four</td>
                        <td>Maps to <span class="@CodeSpan.Base">--br-unit-outline-offset-4</span>.</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                        <td>5</td>
                        <td>Five</td>
                        <td>Maps to <span class="@CodeSpan.Base">--br-unit-outline-offset-5</span>.</td>
                    </tr>
                </tbody>
            </table>
        </div>
    </section>
</section>

<section>
    <h2 class="mobile-centred-heading">Usage</h2>

    <p>
        Below the code section is the result of the code in the section. I added the CodeSpan class as
        an unstyled link colours may not have enough constrast. Link styling class coming soon. Use the tab key or 
        click an hold and move away (so the link does not activate) to see the indicator.
    </p>
    <p>
        Outlines follow the border, so if you wanted a heavily rounded one you could also use the <span class="@CodeSpan.Base">Radius</span>
        class as well. Small bit of rounding coming from the <span class="@CodeSpan.Base">CodeSpan</span> which also has a radius option.
    </p>

    <CodeBox CodeBlock="@CssClassesSnippets.Focus_Outline_Example" AriaLabel="Focus outline code example" />

    <a href="/" class="@FocusOutline.Base @FocusOutline.OnFocus @CodeSpan.Base @CodeSpan.Scheme(CodeSpanScheme.Primary)">Home page link</a>

</section>

